WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.750
llama.

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:07.292
cpp is a low-level local inference ecosystem that supports compatible model formats and multiple hardware backends.

00:00:07.292 --> 00:00:13.017
It offers detailed control and can serve as a foundation for command-line tools, applications,

00:00:13.017 --> 00:00:14.243
and local servers.

00:00:14.243 --> 00:00:18.332
Ollama emphasizes straightforward model management and a local service interface.

00:00:18.332 --> 00:00:22.421
LM Studio provides a desktop experience for discovering, loading, testing,

00:00:22.421 --> 00:00:24.057
and serving supported models.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:27.737
Both can simplify common workflows while retaining runtime-specific limits.

00:00:27.737 --> 00:00:34.279
Open WebUI provides a browser-based interface that can connect to supported local or remote model services.

00:00:34.279 --> 00:00:38.368
Text-generation-webui offers a broader experimental interface at a high level.

00:00:38.368 --> 00:00:42.457
More features also create more dependencies, settings, and security surface.

00:00:42.457 --> 00:00:46.954
Local APIs allow scripts and applications to call a model service.

00:00:46.954 --> 00:00:51.452
Compatibility with a familiar API shape can ease integration, but authentication,

00:00:51.452 --> 00:00:53.497
network binding, request limits, logging,

00:00:53.497 --> 00:00:56.359
and data exposure still require deliberate configuration.

00:00:56.359 --> 00:01:00.039
Model management includes source verification, license review, naming, storage,

00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:04.128
checksums where appropriate, prompt templates, version records, evaluation, and retirement.

00:01:04.128 --> 00:01:09.034
A model file is a software and supply-chain dependency, not just content.

00:01:09.034 --> 00:01:12.714
Start with the simplest tool that meets the requirement.

00:01:12.714 --> 00:01:17.621
Validate one model and workflow before adding orchestration, agents, retrieval, multiple users,

00:01:17.621 --> 00:01:19.257
routing, or distributed services.

00:01:19.257 --> 00:01:21.060
Complexity should follow measured need.
